  "raw_response": "Proxy handling is implemented in `Session.rebuild_proxies`: it removes any existing header, then conditionally regenerates it from proxy-URL credentials. HTTPS requests intentionally do not receive the header to prevent TLS-tunnel leakage.\n\nRelevant files:\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:src/requests/sessions.py?L302-L331](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/src/requests/sessions.py?L302-L331) - Deletes `Proxy-Authorization`; restores it only for non-HTTPS schemes when proxy credentials are present.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:tests/test_requests.py?L641-L669](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/tests/test_requests.py?L641-L669) - Tests preservation on ordinary requests and omission for HTTPS proxy requests.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:src/requests/adapters.py?L592-L611](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/src/requests/adapters.py?L592-L611) - Builds proxy authorization from credentials embedded in the proxy URL.\n- [sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3:HISTORY.md?L224-L228](/r/github.com/sg-evals/requests--v2.32.3/-/blob/HISTORY.md?L224-L228) - Documents the 2.26.0 regression and its fix.",
